    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d41">

                <pb facs="0115" n="25" xml:id="pg25"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/956</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Consul at Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-01-12T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 12,
                                1918, 6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Have any British or Japanese warships reached Vladivostok? Department informed
                    British cruiser <hi rendition="#italic">Suffolk</hi> ordered there from
                    Hongkong. Please advise; also report whether you consider situation requires
                    presence of <hi rendition="#italic">Brooklyn</hi> which is now at Yokohama.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Polk</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
